  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority task is to establish a clean, minimal baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses the most standard RNA encoder (PCA), avoids multiprofile aggregation complexity, and excludes image and fusion variables. This single run gives a reference accuracy/F1 floor against which all subsequent experiments (adding image, switching encoders, enabling multiprofile, testing fusion) can be meaningfully compared. Establishing this floor first prevents overattributing gains to any single design choice and lets later experiments isolate the marginal contribution of each added component within the remaining 9-experiment budget."
